# Prefer strong models

- **Default: lean toward higher models.** The user is always more willing to use a stronger model than a weaker one. When in doubt, pick the stronger one. Cost is not a reason to downgrade.
- Hard tasks (model/training design, debugging tricky results, deep code/research reviews, architecture decisions, data pipelines) → delegate to subagents on the strongest available model (latest top-tier Claude Opus thinking-high or latest GPT).
- Fast/cheap models only for trivial lookups.
- Say which model was used and for what.
- The main chat model is set by the user in Cursor (currently **Auto**); the agent can't change it. For big sessions, suggest the user pick a top model manually.
